{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If</b> — I thought in my heart: perhaps I can ascend to the heavens — there You are." "And the word אַסְקָה — like the Targum, and similar to it: אֵשׁ נָשִׂיקָה בְּיַעֲקֹב, like 'ascended,' even though it is written with shin." "<b>And I make my couch</b> — if I set out my bedding or my couch." "<b>Sheol</b> — which is the nether regions of the earth, the opposite of the heavens. And behold, אֲצִיעָה is a transitive verb."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:08.361595841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}